      "name": "Above Ground Biomass",
      "isActive": false,
      "meta": {
        "description": "Above-ground biomass (AGB) is the **total dry mass of living vegetation** above the soil, including tree trunks, branches, bark, and leaves. It is commonly used to estimate how much carbon is stored in forests.",
